$ whycant read /srv/x

✓ alice (uid 1000) can read /srv/x

  /        drwxr-xr-x  root:root  ✓ traverse
  /srv     drwxr-xr-x  root:root  ✓ traverse
  /srv/x   -rw-r--r--  root:root  ✓ read

Also noticed
  /: running inside a container (docker)
    Results reflect the view from inside this container: its users, mounts and
    files, which can differ from the host's.
  /: running in a user namespace
    uids are mapped (0 100000 65536), so owners and root here are not the host's.
    Files owned by unmapped ids show up as nobody.
